body_text:
At the start of **Winter 1225-26** Wilhelm brings his family to winter at the covenant:
• his father **Carl**, a farmer turned mercenary, who made his money taking a hostage (the man stayed with the family a couple of years until he was ransomed, and is still a good friend) and who is the reason neither son became a soldier;
• his mother **Eloise**, the local miller's daughter and the smart one of the family, from whom the children got their brains;
• his brother **Dietrich**;
• his younger sisters **Angelina**, married in Cologne to a man she met through Dietrich, and **Catherine**, who is considering taking vows.
They fly by **stone sled**: cart-sized stone slabs that carry up to 2,000 lb each, fitted with a light covered wooden frame and flown by hired grogs with **Finesse** (Teamster adds). Someone must be aboard at sunrise and sunset to renew the effect. They follow the coasts rather than fly over forests and towns, so the trip takes two or three days. The **Hound of Cassel** is left free to trade or winter as its captain sees fit.
The covenant watches the procession land beside the wizards' hall. The shipyard is well underway, and grogs drill in the square.
**Rán** comes out to greet them. At first glance she is a blonde woman, until the almost translucent skin and tendril-like hair register, and the family gets a full dose of the uncanny as she plays hostess by a roaring fire over a great spread of grain and fish.
